  https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/fundamentals/package-validation/diagnostic-ids

  Every entry here is a deliberate, reviewed decision. A suppression that nobody can explain is a
  silenced bug, so do not add one without recording why below, and delete one the moment the reason
  stops holding. Regenerating this file with -p:ApiCompatGenerateSuppressionFile=true rewrites it and
  DISCARDS these comments - regenerate into a scratch copy and merge by hand instead.

  Bodu.Financial.ExchangeRates.Boe moves its options onto WebRateProviderOptions in 1.3.0, before
  the package is promoted from Preview to Stable (#1312). BoeEndpointOptions is removed (CP0001):
  its BaseUrl, HttpTimeout and UserAgent are the inherited BaseAddress, HttpTimeout and UserAgent,
  and its QueryPath is BoeRateProviderOptions.QueryPath. BoeRateProviderOptions.Endpoint and
  OnDemandWindowDays are removed (CP0002); the look-back is the inherited DefaultLookback, ten days
  by default. The members BoeRateProviderOptions declared that WebRateProviderOptions also declares
  now come from the base and need no entry. Delete these entries when the Preview validation
  baseline moves past 0.7.x, or when the package takes a Stable baseline.

  FileSystemBoeResponseCache becomes internal in 1.3.0 for the same promotion (#1310), CP0001: no
  public API accepts it, and the disk cache stays reachable through the options' EnableDiskCache and
  CacheDirectory.
-->
